/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 111 0 R
/E (The board is stored as a vector of 9 chars. It starts holding the characters 1 through 9 so the player can see the spot numbers, and those get replaced with X or O as the game goes on. I used a vector instead of a regular array because vectors know their own size, so I can use board.size\(\) instead of hardcoding 9 everywhere.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
